uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.disk.restores"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.disk.restores ~ a pending removal answered toward the records: the file returns

A PENDING REMOVAL names a file that vanished from the path its base names; nothing writes it back and nothing tombstones its records. `restore <uri>…` writes the file back from the records. Name one or more carriers, or `--all --count <n>` for every pending row of the named bag; an answer over more than one carrier names the count that stands pending (read it from `lares shore`), and a count that moved takes nothing.

A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]`; a JSON call off a terminal needs `--yes`, and `--yes` approves nothing by itself. `--face N` answers a lit sibling's pending row without wearing it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ restore-one · restore-all

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`restore-one` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example ~ write the one vanished file back`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`restore-all` params=`all/true count/3 bag/lares ~ write back every pending row of the bag, the count named`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri · all · count · bag · face · yes

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/lar-address seat/1 as/<uri>… ~ one or more carriers a pending removal names`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`all` params=`~ every pending row of the named bag; rides --count`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`count` params=`takes/number ~ the count that stands pending, read from lares shore; an answer over more than one carrier names it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/bag-uri ~ narrow to one bag`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ a lit sibling's shore, by handle index`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`~ name the intent for a call off a terminal; approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/hand ~ the file returns to the host disk; the settling answers run on a person's hand at a terminal`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · count-missing · a-state-that-moved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.restores uri/<uri>]] ~ name a carrier, or --all with --count; --all beside carriers refuses`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`count-missing` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.restores all/true count/3]] ~ an answer over more than one carrier names the count that stands pending`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`a-state-that-moved` params=`~ an answer names the state its giver read (a standoff's key, or the count that stands pending); where that state moved, the island refuses by name and nothing changes`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ restored · aborted

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`restored` params=`exit/0 ~ the file returned from the records`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`aborted` params=`exit/1 ~ the person answered no at the prompt`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares shore restore

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`spells/[[lares shore restore]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

